{"title":"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />-<i>pretty</i> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> has exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> positive divisors and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-pretty. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the sum of positive integers less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f49e1f42131f302f2b4a45393cdc3fed5be2655c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2019$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> that are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-pretty. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/2/882fb30d52831474d9747822b9e91295595fc161.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{S}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"15\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Every 20-pretty integer can be written in form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/6/186000547ff9a91116d13e6815a57a8a3a8cb2db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2^a 5^b k$\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad2cd546ffbb52fe8a7f8e4d1cb3ec38047627e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/3/dc335af40586292a7ea56ec38e63f8010bd42050.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd977fca8a2f7e121904e59264d0e5d4fc9ef99c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(k,10) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/4/964113e30fa0857730ed7315d3aba8948a5ddef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(n) = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/5/b05725a6508fe8df761c6e91d2735b697ebd87d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> is the number of divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Thus, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/6/bf6154cf32400fe57696b1d4c208667534e0de0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 = (a+1)(b+1)d(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"183\" height=\"18\" />, using the fact that the divisor function is multiplicative. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae1ab5a9e4812b64bf188877c0a46d893f2dbac5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+1)(b+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" /> must be a divisor of 20, there are not many cases to check.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c249aabb64e8b8ae488fb60edd19ed406e5a334a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+1 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/e/90e99da7ac7542e3495282db13247ef6cd386824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+1 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />. But this leads to no solutions, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/1/931df6edaff2ec74f47846a90754ea1df4e6a44a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b) = (3,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d4e587f3831d57b538ddceff51aa90df545709c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3 5^4 &gt; 2019$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/3/513f508d155578e28327509142ec495c503e2e9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+1 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/2/4920238c2ec6fbe06c0ea117597942fb0c73f0a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+1 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The first case gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b9342b85649283d841445adc0f9e7a4c956bb82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2^4 \\cdot 5^1 \\cdot p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a prime other than 2 or 5. Thus we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa90a247d10d3f3d3a3894a7e27164a75590f12a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80p &lt; 2019 \\implies p = 3, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"327\" height=\"16\" />. The sum of all such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7943b4b1f9d9e6c353aa50b499670525bb2546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80(3+7+11+13+17+19+23) = 7440$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"334\" height=\"18\" />. In the second case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/1/9b18b339571941800a52fc0638a3326eb7105277.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+1 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/5/fb514e891f3a393312123e446fb7653b67d80a80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(k) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, and there is one solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/673e18b4988fa10e951da0f363d8791b6844bbfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2^4 \\cdot 5^3 = 2000$\" width=\"141\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed99eca9bec35a1d34deb9161b5d21b17b3d96ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+1 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/2/4920238c2ec6fbe06c0ea117597942fb0c73f0a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+1 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, but this gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc770d6bf8d8d8a77dac28ffaeae950f0d293c51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^9 \\cdot 5^1 &gt; 2019$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />. No other values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/b/64be5731bafe97ab8fb5d0f9c52c1c5362f963d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> work.\n</p><p>Then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/a/c8a567232b62c1ac9abcb340f002e9a62e9a94c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S}{20} = \\frac{80(3+7+11+13+17+19+23) + 2000}{20} = 372 + 100 = \\boxed{472}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"548\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>-scrabbler94\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> to have exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> positive divisors, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> can only take on certain prime factorization forms: namely, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c7640eb52be23e2d36a5cb7795962d1d5e1e2f4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^{19}, p^9q, p^4q^3, p^4qr$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/7/3674de20e2b78b5790ea714b9dcaa11af6aa2340.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p,q,r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> are primes. No number that is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed in the first form because 20 has <i>two</i> primes in its prime factorization, while the first form has only <i>one</i>, and the only integer divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> that has the second form is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/0/18022d3c053c325ae0fd43242aa083bd27b56408.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{9}5$\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, which is 2560, greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f49e1f42131f302f2b4a45393cdc3fed5be2655c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2019$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>For the third form, the only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-pretty numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1acd2549fbd11ea1b0ec91fe4692fbbd4352ad08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^45^3=2000$\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/4/0243fbb1368aa3850435707c0f1ad79d50cc16f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^35^4=5000$\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" />, and only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05f1ffc8a6829f25b0b0366087a70dfd4e06fef6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is small enough. \n</p><p>For the fourth form, any number of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524ac8267210ff1a1a3636984040b8628e98eb91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^45r$\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a prime other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> will satisfy the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-pretty requirement. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/0/a908b11e618ad3fe8c8fba2a802c15d23a6ff14d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=80r&lt;2019$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa63d41e3533223414aab2d590f01761c5f1b444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\le 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> can take on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aa62ffe8073088691fd84e9d724ceef50cf4f1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"135\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de5187c08bedbb3a0aa254d4748a302ed1e240a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S}{20}=\\frac{2000+80(3+7+11+...+23)}{20}=100+4(3+7+11+...+23)=\\boxed{472}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"618\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Rephrased for clarity by Afly\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have the number being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/40897a5f887f100131774de71c8690fe0802831f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20k = 2^2 \\cdot 5 \\cdot k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"17\" />. We will consider some cases.\n</p><p>Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> doesn't contain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in its prime factorization\n</p><p>Then let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> divisors and so we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73a3dea0f384f0b093a1a64d1a302cf2d6a85b76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot 2 \\cdot p = 6p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"17\" /> as the total number of divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/a/54af56d0fda10916f0649689e1f22ada0972f9ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20k$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />. Thus must be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/9/af94da38e988a61b2585645f15af37220f942b7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = \\frac{10}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" /> a contradiction. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> must contain either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or both in its prime factorization.\n</p><p>Case 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> but not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in its prime factorization\n</p><p>Then the number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/b/f9b28726cc6f807c21c7ed63ed2e5aef32260963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2 + a} \\cdot 5 \\cdot \\text{something}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" /> assuming <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. That something is the rest of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Let that something have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> factors. Thus we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/b/58bbca0b5fe1acc6ac59b77a6a690cb44ca69ff9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3 + a)(2)(x) = 20 \\implies x(3 + a) = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"304\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/1/9b1838491bea2799f90f459e5a942e9dd6d7c4c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 7$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> which implies the number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/e/13e2ba0687a598cf85108f0fb2e03a6a8e837254.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^9 \\cdot 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> which is too big.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2effc7979b1c93e59356b73253d75e2740b33105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cf0953f43c76a5c79f339f9aee0fc2baac51413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> implying the number must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/f/6df91feba6590dce1ffe409cc69b787cb13e7f22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4 \\cdot 5 \\cdot p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" /> since if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2effc7979b1c93e59356b73253d75e2740b33105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> the rest of the something of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> divisors which is only possible if that something is a prime which we denote here by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> cannot be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Any other divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> has to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> but starting from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43970aa97091f384854d477a1e1e07356887266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> obviously doesn't work. We're done in this case and we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2ea3953009a6e0ccae9b5d21ee09bb7ad0d8c69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2^4 \\cdot 5(3 + 7 + 11 + 13 + 17 + 19 + 23)}{20} = 4(93) = 372$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"418\" height=\"41\" /> in this case.\n</p><p>Case 3: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> but not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in its prime factorization\n</p><p>This case is simple as we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/6/7f656d94823f11cebcf178a75c022e19c48705a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2 \\cdot 5^{1 + a} \\cdot \\text{something}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"20\" /> assuming <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. But the number of total divisors for this number is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> thanks to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a35631e1e126934ead6d2af161e9d250827bbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> term and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> so no cases here.\n</p><p>Case 4: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> contains both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in its prime factorization\n</p><p>Then the number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/3/683d91e24a653409f66705787b63ec7512b733d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2 + a} \\cdot 5^{1 + b} \\cdot \\text{something}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"21\" /> assuming <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Assume that something has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> factors again. Then we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/e/c1e02bdb6cbeaf4ae4bf125f8f2e64090c6b24e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3 + a)(2 + b)x = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"163\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We will do casework noting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dcdf3c228143a3da2d767affe1a2cf24a0d9a72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> must be a divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> that is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is nonnegative. Then we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/d/b1d1bb8c06c598914fb17dba4ed9aeb32051abd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + a = 4, 5, 10, 20 \\implies a = 1, 2, 7, 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"299\" height=\"17\" />. We note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/1/9c19b0a0f727823a736f3d80746d3f91414a6b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> is clearly too big as the final number will be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d13f1b370e2b7652a7f65fabb6028e361459d9db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{19}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> which is clearly way too big. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/1/9b1838491bea2799f90f459e5a942e9dd6d7c4c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 7$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/3/083f114b67b59b74de06b744aecde53ec1af3079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2 + b)x = 2 \\implies b = 0, x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"241\" height=\"20\" /> as the only solution that works if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59bcd486aa4431f6f75e743b0172befdea7f525.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /> are nonnegative. But this doesn't work since this case assumes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> has both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in its prime factorization and if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/7/be7a58270d4285821716c6093a83541f3ea31dc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 0$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> has no factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> a contradiction.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cf0953f43c76a5c79f339f9aee0fc2baac51413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/8/3884057cb53c74653adf7a61e8d6412472e31658.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2 + b)x = 4 \\implies x = 1, b = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"241\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a08b4fd341d944fe77cc80c4534e10c4e9a2bff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2, b = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />. As we know, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a08b4fd341d944fe77cc80c4534e10c4e9a2bff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2, b = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> can't work since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/7/be7a58270d4285821716c6093a83541f3ea31dc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 0$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> doesn't work. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cf0953f43c76a5c79f339f9aee0fc2baac51413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197213da9d06b2c5b59a10ad17f6a4aeb43d6697.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> implies the number has to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/3/ce306dad5c41982041e654bf138e2066a976870f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4 \\cdot 5^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d02444a59b917b64e8bd0963b88712fc7fa0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/a/e7af00da09077815c502a28508b2a7f40b9e2271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2 + b)x = 5 \\implies x = 1, b = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"241\" height=\"20\" />. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/6/8869044d330a23acd026a08d353c9df6f21cd69f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3 \\cdot 5^4 = 5000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"17\" /> which is too big.\n</p><p>So for case 4, we only get one case and that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3391f7106306a447088041d9a256967a77e5fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4 \\cdot 5^3 = 2000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Dividing this by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Finally, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/5/dc5dca790735fcd8fb6b2777c7dcfccfeb86efd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$372 + 100 = \\boxed{472}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"141\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~ilikemath247365\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II\" title=\"2019 AIME II\">2019 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2019 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2019\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2019 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=